WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.490
The GTM Partner Dashboard is a

2
00:00:02.530 --> 00:00:05.021
focused question with a concrete answer:

3
00:00:05.061 --> 00:00:07.551
where is partner revenue coming from,

4
00:00:07.591 --> 00:00:09.660
and what should happen next?

5
00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:12.401
This repository is a static React

6
00:00:12.441 --> 00:00:15.141
mockup for two audiences. GTM leadership

7
00:00:15.181 --> 00:00:17.882
sees the full partner book. An

8
00:00:17.922 --> 00:00:20.622
individual partner sees only the revenue

9
00:00:20.662 --> 00:00:23.363
motions and registrations that belong to

10
00:00:23.403 --> 00:00:26.103
them. Both views use one data

11
00:00:26.143 --> 00:00:26.560
model.

12
00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:29.236
Start with the boundary that keeps

13
00:00:29.276 --> 00:00:31.912
that possible. App creates a data

14
00:00:31.952 --> 00:00:34.588
provider and loads partners, registrations, opportunities,

15
00:00:34.628 --> 00:00:37.265
and targets. The provider returns canonical

16
00:00:37.305 --> 00:00:39.941
dashboard records. The views do not

17
00:00:39.981 --> 00:00:42.617
know whether those records came from

18
00:00:42.657 --> 00:00:45.293
the seeded mock, a CRM, or

19
00:00:45.333 --> 00:00:46.185
a warehouse.

20
00:00:46.225 --> 00:00:48.954
That flow is deliberately small. The

21
00:00:48.994 --> 00:00:51.723
application is a Vite single page

22
00:00:51.763 --> 00:00:54.492
app. Data enters through the provider.

23
00:00:54.532 --> 00:00:57.261
Metrics are derived in a pure

24
00:00:57.301 --> 00:01:00.030
library. React views turn those results

25
00:01:00.070 --> 00:01:02.799
into cards, bars, charts, tables, and

26
00:01:02.839 --> 00:01:03.260
badges.

27
00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:06.520
The domain model has four important

28
00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:09.780
records. Partners identify the account, tier,

29
00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:13.039
region, and manager. Deal registrations capture

30
00:01:13.079 --> 00:01:16.299
a partner estimate and an operations

31
00:01:16.339 --> 00:01:19.559
decision. Opportunities carry the sales-sized amount,

32
00:01:19.599 --> 00:01:22.819
revenue motion, stage, and terminal outcome.

33
00:01:22.859 --> 00:01:25.535
Targets set quarterly revenue expectations.

34
00:01:25.575 --> 00:01:27.967
The registration path is separate from

35
00:01:28.008 --> 00:01:30.400
the sales path. A submission can

36
00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:32.832
be pending, approved, or rejected. An

37
00:01:32.872 --> 00:01:35.265
approved registration can convert into a

38
00:01:35.305 --> 00:01:37.698
Sell With opportunity. The funnel can

39
00:01:37.738 --> 00:01:40.130
show count or registered dollars, but

40
00:01:40.170 --> 00:01:42.563
it never adds a partner estimate

41
00:01:42.603 --> 00:01:44.995
to a later sales-sized opportunity. That

42
00:01:45.035 --> 00:01:47.428
unit boundary is one of the

43
00:01:47.468 --> 00:01:49.860
most important rules in the app.

44
00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:53.066
The leadership view is the operating

45
00:01:53.106 --> 00:01:56.272
dashboard. Eight KPI tiles summarize open

46
00:01:56.312 --> 00:01:59.477
pipeline, closed-won year to date, coverage,

47
00:01:59.517 --> 00:02:02.683
registration approval, registration conversion, win rate,

48
00:02:02.723 --> 00:02:05.889
active partners, and average open deal

49
00:02:05.929 --> 00:02:09.095
size. A type filter changes the

50
00:02:09.135 --> 00:02:12.301
opportunity-derived metrics, stages, revenue trend, and

51
00:02:12.341 --> 00:02:12.835
leaderboard.

52
00:02:12.875 --> 00:02:15.501
The rest of the leadership view

53
00:02:15.541 --> 00:02:18.168
explains why those numbers move. A

54
00:02:18.208 --> 00:02:20.834
registration funnel shows submitted, approved, converted,

55
00:02:20.874 --> 00:02:23.501
rejected, and pending work. A stage

56
00:02:23.541 --> 00:02:26.167
panel shows open opportunities from Discovery

57
00:02:26.207 --> 00:02:28.833
through Deal Desk Review, followed by

58
00:02:28.873 --> 00:02:31.500
won and lost outcomes. Quarterly revenue

59
00:02:31.540 --> 00:02:34.166
is compared with combined partner targets.

60
00:02:34.206 --> 00:02:36.832
A pending queue and leaderboard point

61
00:02:36.872 --> 00:02:38.610
to the next action.

62
00:02:38.650 --> 00:02:41.093
The partner portal applies a stricter

63
00:02:41.133 --> 00:02:43.577
boundary. It removes Sell To opportunities

64
00:02:43.617 --> 00:02:46.060
before rendering anything. The partner can

65
00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:48.543
switch between Total pipeline, Sell With,

66
00:02:48.583 --> 00:02:51.027
and Allocate. That slice changes the

67
00:02:51.067 --> 00:02:53.510
partner KPIs, stage view, and revenue

68
00:02:53.550 --> 00:02:55.993
trend. A separate motion panel keeps

69
00:02:56.033 --> 00:02:58.477
the full visible book in view

70
00:02:58.517 --> 00:03:00.960
so the split is never hidden.

71
00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:03.698
The portal's partner picker is only

72
00:03:03.738 --> 00:03:06.437
a prototype control. Production identity would

73
00:03:06.477 --> 00:03:09.175
come from partner SSO, and the

74
00:03:09.215 --> 00:03:11.913
selected partner would come from the

75
00:03:11.953 --> 00:03:14.652
authenticated session. Registration history is scoped

76
00:03:14.692 --> 00:03:17.390
to that partner and ordered newest

77
00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:20.129
first, with status and rejection reasons

78
00:03:20.169 --> 00:03:20.585
preserved.

79
00:03:20.625 --> 00:03:23.853
The mock book of business is

80
00:03:23.893 --> 00:03:27.120
deterministic. A mulberry32 generator uses seed

81
00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:30.388
20260918, and the snapshot is fixed

82
00:03:30.428 --> 00:03:33.656
at September 18, 2026. The generator

83
00:03:33.696 --> 00:03:36.923
creates 25 partners, 180 registrations, and

84
00:03:36.963 --> 00:03:40.191
roughly 185 opportunities across eight quarters.

85
00:03:40.231 --> 00:03:43.459
The same build produces the same

86
00:03:43.499 --> 00:03:46.726
story, which makes visual review and

87
00:03:46.766 --> 00:03:48.360
future tests repeatable.

88
00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:51.433
The metric layer is where business

89
00:03:51.473 --> 00:03:54.507
rules live. It calculates pipeline, closed-won

90
00:03:54.547 --> 00:03:57.580
revenue, win rate, registration funnel totals,

91
00:03:57.620 --> 00:04:00.653
stage and type breakdowns, target attainment,

92
00:04:00.693 --> 00:04:03.727
coverage, quarterly revenue, pending registrations, and

93
00:04:03.767 --> 00:04:06.800
the partner leaderboard. Views select and

94
00:04:06.840 --> 00:04:09.873
label those results. Shared components stay

95
00:04:09.913 --> 00:04:11.410
focused on rendering.

96
00:04:11.450 --> 00:04:14.184
The project uses a narrow toolchain.

97
00:04:14.224 --> 00:04:16.957
npm runs the Vite development server,

98
00:04:16.997 --> 00:04:19.731
the TypeScript project build, ESLint, and

99
00:04:19.771 --> 00:04:22.504
the production preview. GitHub Actions runs

100
00:04:22.544 --> 00:04:25.278
lint and build on pull requests.

101
00:04:25.318 --> 00:04:28.052
Vercel is the current hosting path

102
00:04:28.092 --> 00:04:30.825
for a private repository, while a

103
00:04:30.865 --> 00:04:33.599
manual Pages workflow remains available if

104
00:04:33.639 --> 00:04:35.910
repository and plan settings change.

105
00:04:35.950 --> 00:04:41.368
The next contributor has clear seams.

106
00:04:41.408 --> 00:04:46.826
Change business calculations in src/lib/metrics.ts. Change

107
00:04:46.866 --> 00:04:52.284
source integration in src/data/DataProvider.ts. Change aggregate

108
00:04:52.324 --> 00:04:57.742
behavior in src/views/LeadershipView.tsx. Change partner visibility

109
00:04:57.782 --> 00:05:03.200
in src/views/PartnerView.tsx. Change reusable presentation in

110
00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:04.110
src/components/.

111
00:05:04.150 --> 00:05:06.602
Remember the architecture as one line:

112
00:05:06.642 --> 00:05:09.095
source records enter through DataProvider, metrics

113
00:05:09.135 --> 00:05:11.587
give them meaning, and two views

114
00:05:11.627 --> 00:05:14.079
expose the right slice for each

115
00:05:14.119 --> 00:05:16.572
audience. That is the whole dashboard,

116
00:05:16.612 --> 00:05:19.064
and it is small enough to

117
00:05:19.104 --> 00:05:20.310
understand before changing.
